{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792692897,"nonce":"bSbTWPEf2K1xkyrxa1BhWiJoqC0=","title":"Raw images discard rounded clip corner shapes and overflow fades","message":"Remaining clip-property audit under raw-image parent 369499d9d754d8353823d4eb9ff5ff76e5469007b2983e58b3a677f88b5bbc6c. Circle/ellipse/polygon geometry is handled by d5ef50d, and raw path geometry by 265d822; ordinary rectangular/circular-rounded clipping and empty rejection predate those fixes.\n\nCode audit: emit_rgba_pixels discards get_clip_data's corner-shape vector and never captures get_clip_fade. Rectangular/rounded raw images keep empty clip_aux, so their clip radii reach the image pipeline but native per-corner superellipse exponents and overflow fades do not. Nonrectangular image headers also currently leave fade rows at zero. These properties therefore remain outside the completed shape-geometry slices.\n\nAdd independent offscreen controls for shaped rounded corners (including asymmetric corner shapes), overflow-fade distances and their clip frame before implementation. Preserve the push-time/draw-time coordinate conventions already established by native painting, ancestor stripping, empty rejection, tight origins, ownership and cache invalidation. Reuse the image pipeline where possible; shared ClipPath/CSS changes remain owner-gated. This issue records a source audit, not newly verified pixel or performance results.","files":null}]}